**<span class="mark">Gastric sleeve surgery in Perth, a straightforward
guide from a team you can trust</span>**

<span class="mark">If you are one of the [<u>75% of West
Australians</u>](https://www.health.wa.gov.au/~/media/Corp/Documents/Health-for/Nutrition-monitoring-survey-series/2022/Weight-and-Health_FINAL.pdf)
living with overweight or obesity and are exploring different types of
bariatric surgery, you may be considering a sleeve gastrectomy (gastric
sleeve surgery). Weight loss surgery is a big decision, often after
years of unsuccessful weight loss and regain and all the emotional
challenges that accompany it. Yet in the right hands, gastric sleeve
surgery is a safe, powerful, and lasting weight loss tool.</span>

### **<span class="mark">What is a gastric sleeve?</span>**

<span class="mark">A sleeve gastrectomy, commonly known as gastric
sleeve surgery, is a surgical procedure that reduces the size of your
stomach by up to 75-80%. The ‘sleeve’ is created by constructing a
narrow banana-shaped tube from your stomach. It is typically performed
‘laparoscopically’ via keyhole surgery, which tends to mean an easier
recovery than some more invasive procedures.</span>

<span class="mark">Gastric sleeve surgery is highly effective for weight
loss for two key reasons: first, because your stomach is smaller, you
feel fuller, faster. Secondly, because a reduced stomach size minimises
your body’s production of ghrelin (the ‘hunger hormone’), after gastric
sleeve surgery, your appetite will also be reduced.</span>

<span class="mark">As the gastric sleeve procedure is permanent, your
surgeon will help you understand the risks and benefits, and your
suitability based on your weight and whether or not you are experiencing
any associated health conditions.</span>

